  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4cos\u2061x+2sin\u2061x)=$",
  "worked_solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin\u2061x)=cos\u2061x,$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos\u2061x)=-sin\u2061x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4cos\u2061x+2sin\u2061x) & =4(-sin\u2061x)+2(cos\u2061x) \\\\  & =2cos\u2061x-4sin\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
